            </profile>
            <profile id="1f41-2e77-08b9-6cad" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="15ea-5299-d0f5-5dbb" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapon and light armour. Rides a horse. May have heavy armour (+1 pt), bow (+3 pts) and either kontos &amp; buckler (+3 pts), or shield (+2 pts). The horse may be barded (+4 pts). Army General. The Shahanshah may only be chosen for armies exceeding 2,000 pts. Shahanshahs and Spahbedhs may dismount (-3 pts, reduce Movement to 4), and be seated on a Throne. Either character may be upgraded to WS5, S4 and 3 attacks for +20 pts. Later Sassanian army general options may have half-barding (+2 pts) and thrusting spear (+2 pts). 0-1 Army General (with the Spahbedh). (Byzantium p.47)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="f137-363f-08a9-eac0" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">6+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
