  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="38bf-29c2-cb27-bd99" name="Sassanid Persians (Byzantium) - List Notes" publicationId="15ea-5299-d0f5-5dbb" hidden="false">
      <description>SASSANID PERSIANS (Byzantium: Beyond the Golden Gate, pp.44-49). Special rules: CANE SHIELDWALL: troops armed with Cane Shields count as being armed with large shields; formed troops with Cane Shields may form a shieldwall instead of moving (-1 to be hit from the front, as long as they do not move or lose a round of combat); if a unit armed with Cane Shields flees they abandon their shields for the rest of the battle. Later Sassanid special rules: Lakhmid Arab cavalry count as Ld 6 (-2 pts); any unit of Later Sassanian Clibanarii may exchange buckler for thrusting spear and shield (+2 pts); Later Sassanian Clibanarii may dismount (-9 pts, reduce Movement to 4; no Jurz maces); characters, Regular and Royal Clibanarii may have half-barding (+2 pts). Light cavalry share a separate allowance in the Cavalry total.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Sassanid Persians - Early Sassanid Persians]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: at least 50%
  Light Cavalry: up to 50%
  Infantry: up to 25%
  Special Units: up to 25%
  Allies and Mercenaries: up to 25%
  EARLY SASSANID PERSIANS. Characters up to 25%; Cavalry at least 50% (up to 50% of the points may be spent on light cavalry; Light Clibanarii may not be chosen); Infantry up to 25%; Special Units up to 25%; Allies and Mercenaries up to 25%. Early Sassanid Persians are Used to Elephants. Armies led by the Spahbedh may include one unit of Royal Clibanarii; armies led by the Shahanshah up to three.
[Sassanid Persians - Later Sassanid Persians]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: at least 50%
  Light Cavalry: up to 25%
  Infantry: up to 33%
  Special Units: up to 25%
  Allies and Mercenaries: up to 25%
  LATER SASSANID PERSIANS. Characters up to 25%; Cavalry at least 50% (up to 25% of the points may be spent on light cavalry; Cataphracts and Ephthalites may not be chosen); Infantry up to 33%; Special Units up to 25%; Allies and Mercenaries up to 25%. Later Sassanid Persians are Used to Elephants. Armies led by the Spahbedh may include up to three units of Royal Clibanarii; armies led by the Shahanshah any amount.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
